# CHANGELOG discipline

We follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/) format. Single `CHANGELOG.md` at repo root.

## When to update

| Change size              | Action                                                   |
| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| < 50 LOC, internal only  | No CHANGELOG entry needed                                |
| < 50 LOC, public-facing  | One-liner under `[Unreleased]`                            |
| ≥ 50 LOC                 | Required entry with section (Added/Changed/Fixed/Removed) |
| New tool added           | REQUIRED entry under `### Added` with tool name          |
| New category             | REQUIRED entry + sub-bullet of approximate tool count    |
| Breaking change          | REQUIRED entry under `### Changed` with migration note   |
| Phase boundary           | Move `[Unreleased]` content under new version heading    |

## Format

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

### Added
- New tool `draw_circle_by_3_points` in `acad-geometry-2d` (#42)
- Validator rule `PN-EN-ISO-128-line-weights` in `acad-validators`

### Changed
- `LayerInfo.Color` is now nullable - older drawings without explicit color now report null instead of 7 (white)

### Deprecated
- Tool `move_entity` (use `move_entities` for batched, identical performance for n=1)

### Removed
- (nothing this cycle)

### Fixed
- Race condition in `UiThreadDispatcher` queue when AutoCAD is shutting down

### Security
- Named pipe ACL tightened to current user only (was: Authenticated Users)
```

## Rules

- Add entries at TOP of `[Unreleased]` section
- One bullet per change (no walls of text)
- Reference issue/PR with `(#NN)` when applicable
- Past tense ("Added X", "Fixed Y")
- Include tool/category/file context so the reader knows what to look at
